{"parentUuid":"fe2b84ea-ea4b-4dc3-a9e0-0874f8c06761","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdwmrizV4V7CqXg8oRKqu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The change:\n\n**`src/builtin.c:645`** — the unreserved set for `@uri` now matches RFC 3986 §2.3:\n```c\nconst char* p = CHARS_ALPHANUM \"-_.~\";\n```\nPreviously it was `\"-_.!~*'()\"` (RFC 2396's unreserved set, which also included the \"mark\" characters `!*'()`). Those four now get percent-encoded.\n\n**`tests/jq.test`** — updated the existing combined-format expectation (`'` → `%27`) and added two cases: a round-trip of the full unreserved set, and encoding of the reserved/other ASCII punctuation.\n\n**Docs** — `docs/content/manual/manual.yml` now cites RFC 3986 and lists the unreserved characters; I hand-applied the matching change to the checked-in `jq.1.prebuilt` using its existing roff escaping conventions (`\\-`, `\\.`). `tests/man.test` needs no regeneration — the `@uri` text lives in prose, not in an `examples:` block.\n\nOne thing I could not do: **I did not build or run the test suite.** This tree has no `configure` (only `configure.ac`), and `autoreconf -i` was denied by the permission layer, as was executing any locally compiled binary. So the new test expectations are verified by manual ASCII-code review of the changed code path, not by an actual run. If you grant approval for `autoreconf`/`make`, I'll build and run `make check` to confirm.\n\nNote this is a user-visible behavior change: `@uri` output for `!`, `*`, `'`, `(`, `)` differs from jq 1.6, so anything comparing against previously generated URLs will see `%21`, `%2A`, `%27`, `%28`, `%29` instead. That's the intent of the RFC 3986 alignment, but it's worth a NEWS mention — I left NEWS alone since it currently only has per-release sections with no unreleased entry to append to."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":26020,"output_tokens":742,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":742,"cache_read_input_tokens":26020,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":369},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdwmrhmZVLLEG6ika7aMt","type":"assistant","uuid":"5db468e3-a177-466b-bf9b-c1d14d329243","timestamp":"2026-08-11T22:47:00.857Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"__CODEX_BAKEOFF_SAMPLE_REPOSITORY__","sessionId":"a0db12e1-6603-4706-92f6-cf2a8c61912c","version":"2.1.224","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
